xgameruntime: complete runtime calls after they return, as the GDK does, and never call a completion routine that is not code.

Forza Horizon 6 crashed during its online session (network_session/coordinator) with two threads on one freed object:
the main thread copying a std::function out of it (exe+3217541, manager read as 1) and a thread-pool thread calling
a completion routine at address 1 from invoke_async_completion. xgr_async_complete_ex answered calls such as
XNetworkingQuerySecurityInformationForUrlAsync (asked before every libHttpClient request) inside the call itself;
libHttpClient is written for the Windows order (the block reads pending when the call returns). The answer is now
published and the completion delivered from the thread pool after the call returns (XGR_INLINE_COMPLETIONS=1 brings
back the old behaviour), and a routine that is neither in a mapped image nor in executable memory is refused with
an ERR naming the block and who began or completed it. Applied by tools/mac_fix_xasync_inline.sh.

